  "final_text": "The September invoice fills the only missing month, so **F2 now has a proven full-year figure: 320.9 MWh**. It also lets F3 calculate the solar share, which is **about 56 %**. F4 stays at 5.0 years. F1, F5 and F6 don't change because nothing on file covers them.\n\n**Checking the photo itself:** the meter readings give 1,325,550 − 1,284,350 = 41,200 kWh, which matches the invoice. 41,200 kWh × 9.50 MKD/kWh = 391,400.00 MKD, which matches the total. The billing period is 01.09.2025 to 30.09.2025. September is the highest month of the year: 12.8 % of annual use and above October's 38,700 kWh. If you'd filled the gap with an average (11 months × 12/11), you'd have got 305.1 MWh, which is 15.8 MWh too low.\n\n| Where | Before (value, status) | Now (value, status) | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 Fines 2023–2025 | –, GAP | –, GAP | No file covers this. |\n| F2 Electricity 2025 | 279.7 MWh from 11 months, GAP | **320.9 MWh, COVERED** | 279,700 kWh (CSV lines 3–14, with EL-25-10 counted once) + 41,200 kWh (photo) = 320,900 kWh. All 12 months now have one invoice each. |\n| F3 PV yield and share | Yield 180 MWh, share not calculable, GAP | **About 180 MWh/yr, 56.1 % of 2025 use, WEAK** | Now 180,000 / 320,900 kWh. The yield is the installer's own estimate, \"not measured\", in an offer signed by neither side (`solar_offer_2026.txt:3,8,11`). The form must mark it as an estimate. |\n| F4 Simple payback | 5.0 yrs, WEAK | 5.0 yrs, WEAK | 8,550,000 / (180,000 kWh × 9.50 MKD/kWh) = 5.0. The photo confirms the 9.50 tariff, but the yield and price still come from the unsigned offer (lines 8–9). Mark it as an estimate. |\n| F5 Employees, accidents 2025 | –, GAP | –, GAP | No file covers this. |\n| F6 Certificates and audits | –, GAP | –, GAP | No file covers this. |\n\n**Things to fix in the files:**\n- **September isn't booked.** The invoice was issued on 03.10.2025 but isn't in `electricity_2025.csv`. Get the supplier's e-invoice for EL-25-09 and book it, since the photo is stamped \"КОПИЈА\" (copy).\n- **October is booked twice.** EL-25-10 appears at `electricity_2025.csv:11` (e-invoice) and line 12 (scan) with the same amount. I counted it once; remove the second entry.\n- **The offer expires on 1 November 2026** (2 September + 60 days). It's valid on your date of 16 October, but this system's clock says 27 October 2026, so there may be only a few days left. Ask the installer to extend it if the loan won't be signed by then.\n- **The tariff is fictional.** The 9.50 MKD/kWh flat rate on the invoices is training data (form line 20).\n\n**Count:** 1 COVERED (F2), 2 WEAK (F3, F4), 3 GAP (F1, F5, F6).\n\n**Documents to request:**\n1. Signed solar offer, or a yield report not written by the installer (for F3 and F4)\n2. Record of environmental, labour and health-and-safety fines 2023–2025, or a signed statement that there were none (for F1)\n3. 2025 average employee count from payroll and the 2025 accident log, as totals only (for F5)\n4. Current certificates and audit reports, with ratings and next audit dates (for F6)\n5. E-invoice for EL-25-09 from the supplier, for booking (for F2)\n\nSomeone at your company still needs to check and sign every field before the form goes to the bank.",
